{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>The wing of the rananim</b> — the name of a bird; perhaps it is so called because of the pleasantness of its voice." "<b>She flutters</b> (נעלסה) — like <b>she spreads</b> (נפרשה). So too: <b>she flutters in loves</b> (נתעלסה באהבים). And the meaning: Do you give the rananim a wing, and give her pinion — it is the wing. So too: <b>He bears him on His pinion</b> (ישאהו על אברתו). And <b>and the stork</b> likewise refers to a bird that comes at a known time, for thus it is written in the book of Isaiah."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {1 "The second biblical quote (נתעלסה באהלים) appears to be from Ezekiel 16:33 (נתעלסי באהבים); Ibn Ezra quotes it with slight variation in spelling and gender. The third quote (ישאהו על אברתו) is from Deuteronomy 32:11. The final reference to Isaiah likely concerns the stork's migration (Isaiah 38:14 or similar)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:05:15.872336170Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}